      "answer": "$\\dfrac83$ square units.",
      "official_mark_scheme_text": "For all methods: $x=\\pm1$ — B1*; both $x$-coordinates for the intersection points.\nMethod 1: subtract and attempt to integrate — M1*.\n$\\int(-2x^2+2)\\,dx=-\\dfrac23x^3+2x$ — B1*; both terms correct.\nApply their positive and negative intersection limits to their integrated expression — M1.\n$\\dfrac83$ — DB1; accept $2\\dfrac23$ or AWRT $2.67$ WWW; condone $-\\dfrac83\\to\\dfrac83$.\nMethod 2: attempt to integrate both functions and subtract — M1*; the second integral may be replaced with their trapezium area.\n$\\{-\\dfrac23x^3+4x^2+11x\\}-\\{4x^2+9x\\}$ — B1* OE; all terms correct. The second integral may be replaced by $\\dfrac12(1+17)\\times2$ OE.\nApply their positive and negative intersection limits to both expressions — M1; if a trapezium is used, replace the second integral by their $18$.\n$\\dfrac83$ — DB1; same numerical guidance.\nMethod 3: subtract and attempt to integrate — M1*.\n$-\\dfrac23(x-2)^3-4x^2+10x$ — B1*; all terms correct.\nApply their limits — M1.\n$\\dfrac83$ — DB1.\nMethod 4: attempt to integrate and subtract — M1*; second integral may be their trapezium area.\n$\\{-\\dfrac23(x-2)^3+19x\\}-\\{4x^2+9x\\}$ — B1*; all terms correct.\nApply their limits — M1; if a trapezium is used, replace the second integral by their $18$ OE.\n$\\dfrac83$ — DB1; same guidance.\nSC B1 for mistaking the triangle for a trapezium leading to $\\dfrac{11}{3}$, i.e. a total of $2/5$.\nTotal: 5",
